{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he drew off his shoe.</b> Boaz drew off his shoe and gave it to the redeemer. Now this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, called חליפין [exchange]. The reason: acceptance of this shoe — and you have given your redemption in its stead. And the reason for a shoe: because it is always present, and it is not possible to remove a garment or trousers lest one remain exposed. And some say that the redeemer drew off his shoe and gave it to Boaz, the meaning being: just as I have given you this shoe, so the redemption."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's parenthetical gloss on חליפין is omitted; the term is left in Hebrew as a technical legal designation, consistent with the discipline of preserving technical terminology."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:35.546970289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}